<h2 id="filters">Filter and sort the table</h2>
<p class="sub">The table below has 76 rows. <strong>Hide lands</strong> shows only spells. <strong>Hide already at 4-of</strong> shows only cards you still need (a "playset" is 4 copies because that's the deck-building limit). <strong>Hide rotating next cycle</strong> drops cards from the sets leaving Standard at the next rotation, so a wildcard you spend now stays legal for the full season. Those are Wilds of Eldraine (WOE) and Lost Caverns of Ixalan (LCI), the 2023 sets that rotate out in the fall 2026 cycle. All three filters start ON; click a lit button to turn it off. For sorting, use the <strong>Wildcards needed</strong> and <strong>Deck count</strong> buttons, or click any column header. (Win rate is a per-deck number, not a per-card one, so its sort lives down in the 25-deck section below.)</p>
