<h2 id="ranking">The craft ranking (76 candidates)</h2>
<p class="sub"><strong>How to read each column.</strong> <em>Rank</em> is the sort position. <em>Card</em> is the card name (bold = you don't own a playset yet). <em>CI</em> is "color identity", which colors the card uses; "C" means colorless (any deck can use it). <em>Rarity</em> tells you which wildcard pile to spend from. <em>Set</em> is the 3-letter code of the expansion the card is in. <em>Type</em> is creature, artifact, land, etc. <em>MV</em> is mana value (what it costs to play). <em>Owned</em> is how many copies you currently have on Arena. <em>WC to 4-of</em> is how many wildcards it would cost to finish a playset. <em>Most shared crafts</em> is the headline number: if you craft this card, how many of the 25 popular decks actually run it, a real count from 1 to 25 pulled from Untapped decklists (not color legality). Quantity does not matter, one copy or four, the question is only whether each deck plays the card. A higher number means crafting it helps more of your decks, so each wildcard does more work. Cards at 0 are ones no current Mardu-color deck plays.</p>

